# ── Reiwa OS environment ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The app runs out-of-the-box with an embedded, file-persistent Postgres
# (PGlite) — no configuration required for local development. The variables
# below are optional / for the production Supabase path.

# Auth: HMAC secret for session cookies. Defaults to an insecure dev value.
# SET THIS in any shared/production environment.
AUTH_SECRET=

# Local DB persistence directory (default: ./.data/pg)
# PGLITE_DATA_DIR=

# ── Production (Supabase) — future path ──────────────────────────────────────
# The same migrations in supabase/migrations/ apply to a hosted Postgres.
# Point a Postgres driver / Supabase client at these, then the RLS helper
# functions in migration 0001 can read auth.jwt() claims instead of GUCs.
# DATABASE_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
